<title>SINGAPORE: Koh Brothers 96 net profit down 6 pct.</title>
<headline>Koh Brothers 96 net profit down 6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				9.00  vs   9.58</p>
<p>Dividend (cents)			0.90  vs   0.80</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     3.78  vs   4.03</p>
<p>    Turnover				249.97  vs 213.69</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 0.11  vs   0.11</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    3.21  vs   2.38</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		6.51  vs   5.62</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 13.98  vs  13.79</p>
<p>    Tax					 5.13  vs   4.07</p>
<p>    Minorities		     (gain) 0.15  vs   0.13 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		(loss) 0.90  vs   nil</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		     July 23, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:		   July 8, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Koh Brothers Group Ltd is involved in construction and building materials.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
